# Copy to .dev.vars for local `wrangler dev` / `wrangler dev --test-scheduled`.
# Never commit the real values (.dev.vars is gitignored).
#
# The HRPT sync's storage backend is Cloudflare D1 (see the `d1_databases`
# binding in wrangler.jsonc), accessed via the `env.DB` Workers binding —
# not a REST URL + bearer token, so there is no secret to set here for it.
# `wrangler dev` automatically provisions a local D1 simulation for the
# `DB` binding; run `wrangler d1 migrations apply spordo-hrpt --local` once
# to apply migrations/0001_init.sql to it.
#

# The Socrata (tvpp-9vvx) sync's storage backend is Supabase (NOT D1 — see
# CLAUDE.md's "Storage is split" section), reached over PostgREST via plain
# `fetch` (src/socrata/supabaseClient.js, src/socrataPermitsApi.js). Copy
# this file to .dev.vars and fill in real values for local `wrangler dev` /
# `wrangler dev --test-scheduled`. Never commit the real values.

# Required. Service-role key for the Supabase project at SUPABASE_URL (see
# the "vars" block in wrangler.jsonc for the URL, which is not secret).
# Get it from Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> service_role
# secret. This bypasses Row Level Security -- it must NEVER be used in
# client code (public/TrueSpordo.html uses the separate, public anon key
# only) and must NEVER be committed.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Recommended, not strictly required. A Socrata app token raises the
# per-IP/per-token rate limit well above the shared anonymous limit.
# Register one at https://data.cityofnewyork.us/profile/app_tokens (free,
# requires a Socrata/NYC Open Data account) and paste it here. The sync
# still runs without this set (src/socrata/fetchSocrata.js logs a warning
# and proceeds anonymously) -- but expect 429s under any real load without it.
SOCRATA_APP_TOKEN=
